    "notes": "The north Renaissance wall has stacked open loggias over the outlying hillside stone base. The inner face has the projecting open spiral staircase. Louis XII’s gate range combines brick with carved pale surrounds; Gaston d’Orléans faces the court in classical pale masonry. The medieval hall and chapel retain steep roofs."
